  31: 
  32: ## WHICH OF MY PROPOSED DISPOSITIONS IS WRONG -- answered first, and it is not the one flagged
  33: 
  34: The brief steered me hardest at **D3/D4 (Part A)** and **E3 (Part B)** -- the disclose-not-row dispositions.  I checked
  35: all three against the measuring seat's own measurements and **all three are CORRECT**.  The wrong dispositions are the
  36: two I was NOT asked to doubt, because they are in my OWN PRIOR RULING -- exactly the place a ruling in my favour hides:
  37: 
  38: 1. **PART A, prior RA3: "the `d->warned`-keyed shrink is clause (e) by the DEPENDS-ON bound."  WRONG -- it is FLOOR.**
  39:    This is the coordinator's D7, handed to me ungraded.  I rule FLOOR (S-A.7 below).  RA3 scoped "the guarded body" to
  40:    the two ACCEPT arms; the governing rule (pass-11 floor definition) keys on *"device-STATE lvalues the fix's own
  41:    repair path reads,"* and the fix's repair path -- the `else`/decline arm at `dev_sgi_ip32.c:314` -- reads `d->warned`,
  42:    in a hunk this very diff adds.  My prior RA1 already flagged RA3 as "disputed, carried to the next adjudication."
  43:    This is that adjudication.
  44: 
  45: 2. **PART B, prior RB1's lane-1/lane-2 channel choices: "lane 1 R and W: CMOS REG C ...; lane 2 reads ...: IIR."
  46:    WRONG -- both are one-shot LATCHES.**  A latch separates zero accesses from at-least-one; it can never separate one
  47:    from two, which is the entire question a forward-COUNT class asks (`opus_c5.../OPUS_ANSWER.md` s2, measured: `WWall`
  48:    169/185, `RWall` 167/185, `RD2post` 161/185 all stub-only at those lanes).  Repair 6 uses the 8253 alternators
  49:    instead.  RB1's *"lanes 0-2 must not rest solely on the stub"* PRINCIPLE was right; the CHANNELS I named to satisfy
  50:    it could not.
  51: 
  52: **D3, D4 and E3 stand** (S-A.3, S-A.4, S-B.3).  The measuring seat independently reached the same disposition on each,
  53: and each has an independent second reason.  The coordinator's instinct that a convenient disclosure was hiding
  54: somewhere was correct; the disclosure that was actually mis-graded was mine, from the last round, in the other direction
  55: (disclosing what should be rowed).  **Count the arguments, not the seats: in both parts a MEASURED clean sweep the
  56: reading seats did not engage with outweighs the CLOSES/GO verdicts, exactly as last round.**
