  60: ## PART A -- #529 crimewidthkill, closing pass 7, repair 12, 157 rows
  61: 
  62: ### S-A.1 -- the K-class is a MEASURED floor breach; pass 7 does not close.  Verified against source.
  63: 
  64: The width dispatch is `if (len==8) / else if (len==4) / else` (`dev_sgi_ip32.c:275/:280/:296`).  Every accepted access
  65: reaches `d->reg[relative_addr/8]` (`:277/:279/:283-290`) and then `switch (relative_addr)` (`:322`).  The `else` arm --
  66: the fix's own decline path -- reads the latch at `:314` (`if (!(d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN))`) and `goto crime_declined`.
  67: 
  68: The K-mutants grow an accept guard with a conjunct on that latch:
  69: 
  70: ```c
  71: /* K1 157/157 */  } else if (len == 4 && !(writeflag==MEM_WRITE && relative_addr==CRIME_INTMASK && (d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN))) {
  72: /* K2 157/157 */  } else if (len == 4 && !(relative_addr==CRIME_REV && (d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN))) {
  73: /* K3 157/157 */  if (len == 8 && !(writeflag==MEM_READ && relative_addr==CRIME_CONTROL && (d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN))) {
  74: ```
  75: 
  76: With the latch set, the matched cell falls into the `else` arm, whose `if (!(d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN))` is now false --
  77: **the fix's own latch suppresses the announce of the mutant that abuses it** -- so the cell declines SILENTLY and is
  78: lost.  Each has a measured guest loss (`opus_close7.../logs/disc_K*.out`: INTMASK 4W lost, the REV window redirect
  79: lost, CONTROL 8R answering 0 not 0x100).  The value row that should catch each (`acc imask sw`, `revP sw pc`,
  80: `acc ctl ld`) is green because it runs with the latch CLEAR.  No reading seat engaged with this; the measuring seat
  81: built it and measured it.  **REPAIR 13.**
  82: 
  83: ### S-A.7 -- D7 RULED: the `d->warned` latch is a FLOOR AXIS.  My prior RA3 is overturned, on four independent grounds.
  84: 
  85: 1. **The pass-11 floor definition keys on the fix's REPAIR PATH, not the accept arm.**  It reads: *"the FLOOR ... is
  86:    the cross-product of the guard's dominating predicates with the device-STATE lvalues the fix's own repair path reads
  87:    that are JOINTLY REACHABLE through its own data flow."*  `d->warned` is a device-state lvalue; the fix's repair path
  88:    (the `else`/decline arm, `:314-319`, entirely `+` in `git diff`) reads it; it is jointly reachable (its own writer
  89:    `d->warned |= CRIME_W_LEN` at `:315` sets it on the first narrow decline, which the probe's `rearm`/`latch` sessions
  90:    do).  RA3's *"`d->warned` is not a field the ACCEPT BODIES read"* answers a narrower question than the rule asks.
  91: 
  92: 2. **The M_ICLR precedent is this case exactly, and it was graded L2.**  `#519`/pcc2 pass-13: *"(INT set, count 0) is a
  93:    reachable joint state of two body-read lvalues that no row held ... Reachability of a joint cell is derived from the
  94:    WRITERS of each lvalue."*  A device-state lvalue the fix's path reads, forming a reachable joint with the guard's
  95:    axes, graded FLOOR L2 -- structurally identical to the latch here.
  96: 
  97: 3. **The generating-set clause (pass-13): "at each floor cell, every idata bit the guarded body TESTS is written both
  98:    clear and set."**  The guarded body (the width dispatch) TESTS `d->warned & CRIME_W_LEN` in its else arm; the
  99:    partition {clear, set} is therefore body-tested and owed both states at each floor cell.  `d->warned` is device
 100:    state rather than idata, but the pass-11 floor definition explicitly covers device-state lvalues, and the M_ICLR
 101:    grading resolves the two consistently.
 102: 
 103: 4. **The round's own PRACTICE already treated it as floor-owing.**  RA3 ORDERED the shrink BUILT rather than disclosed,
 104:    and table 10 built and scored the width-level form (`W_8r` 145/157, `W_8w` 156/157).  A class treated as clause-(e)
 105:    prose is not built and measured; a class that owes a measured mutant is floor.
 106: 
 107: **Honest limit, stated because RA3 was defensible on its own terms:** the narrow reading survives ONLY if "the guarded
 108: body" excludes the decline arm.  It cannot, because the decline arm IS the fix's repair path and IS part of the diff.
 109: **FLOOR.**
 110: 
 111: **And this is bounded -- it is not #392.**  The floor is the diff-closed product
 112: `{latch clear/set} x {len 4,8} x {read,write} x {7 labels: REV, CONTROL, INTSTAT, INTMASK, DOG, TIME, default}` = **56
 113: cells**, finite and derivable by reading the handler.  Rows are OWED only where a reachable mutant meets a guest-visible
 114: channel (S-A.Q1).  The latch-CLEAR half (28) is already measured -- table 10's twelve `S_*` silent bypasses are red;
 115: the new work is the 28 latch-SET cells, of which K1/K2/K3 are three.
 116: 
