 327:   THE DECLINE-SUPPRESSION FACE.  The `goto crime_declined' SKIPS the register switch, and what it skips is
 328:   an OMISSION -- it reads, writes and tests nothing -- so every floor clause in this project enumerates the
 329:   EMPTY SET over it.  Two mutants that condition the `goto' on a LABEL score 188/188 against this probe:  [188-row]
 330:       M3_timelatch   the goto moved inside the latch block, exempting CRIME_TIME  -- 188/188  [188-row]
 331:       M5_revlatch    the same at CRIME_REV                                        -- 188/188  [188-row]
 332:   with M4_timeplain (the same edit WITHOUT the latch conjunct) killed at 184/188 and M6_istlatch (the same  [188-row]
 333:   edit at INTSTAT) killed at 185/188 -- the controls that make those two escapes mean `no row looked'.  [188-row]
 334:   *** OF THE FIVE GUEST-OBSERVABLE LABELS ON THAT FACE, THREE HAVE BEEN SWEPT (INTSTAT killed, TIME and REV
 335:   escaping) AND **INTMASK AND CONTROL-WRITE ARE COVERED ONLY BY READING, NEVER MEASURED**.  Deriving them
 336:   covered is the same move that M5_revlatch was built to punish: REV was DERIVED open and then MEASURED
 337:   open. ***  Carriers for TIME and REV, and label-swap mutants for INTMASK and CONTROL-write, are OWED and
 338:   are not in this file yet.
